  "details": "The RPM Package Manager (RPM) is a command-line driven package management system capable of installing, uninstalling, verifying, querying, and updating software packages.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * rpm: Command injection in rpmuncompress via unescaped filenames passed to popen() (CVE-2026-84838)\n  * rpm: Command Injection in `rpmbuild -t*` (`getTarSpec`) via Unescaped Tarball Path (CVE-2026-84837)\n  * rpm: Command Execution via Macro Expansion in `rpmuncompress -x` for Crafted `.gem` Filenames (CVE-2026-84233)\n  * rpm: rpmbuild getTarSpec() crafted tar member name ? macro injection (CVE-2026-78367)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
